they've gone up over the last several years. So it's not like we have a period where we are experiencing intense stress and then that calms down and we have a break. It has been constant. And if you look at both the political environment, you look at the economic environment, you look at the social environment, those stressors have been constant. So the issue isn't how do we lean more into those break periods? We just don't have those break periods. So we have to, as people, have ways of coping and strategizing around how we deal with stress. So that means that we, first of all, we need to understand it.
在过去几年里它们一直在上升。所以这并不是说我们有一个经历强烈压力然后平静下来并休息一段时期的时期。它一直是恒定的。如果你看看政治环境，看看经济环境，看看社会环境，那些压力源一直是恒定的。所以问题不在于我们如何更多地倾斜到那些休息期。我们根本没有那些休息期。因此，作为人，我们必须有应对和制定战略的方法，围绕我们如何处理压力。这意味着我们首先需要理解它。

